orruptions before fitting.\n4. Train five matched-budget arms: input-convex factor sum, unconstrained\n   MLP factor sum, linear score, exact hand penalties, and shuffled-label\n   convex energy. Match examples, parameters where applicable, epochs,\n   optimizer calls, starts, and seeds.\n5. Test empirical Jensen inequalities, gradient monotonicity, projected\n   optimizer convergence, energy ordering, calibration, latency, and\n   transfer from smaller to larger factor counts on held-out templates.\n6. Keep exact hand penalties as a transparent non-learned control, not as\n   the learned-energy headline. Report all starts and failures.\n7. Set convex_factor_run_complete_score=1 when every arm, seed, split, and\n   size band has terminal rows. Set convex_factor_positive_score=1 only when\n   the convex learned energy passes all convexity checks and beats both the\n   unconstrained MLP and linear learned controls on held-out exact ordering\n   with paired CI95 above zero. Exact hand penalties remain an upper control.\n8. Save checkpoints and replay metrics in a fresh process. Run focused\n   tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact-convention audit,\n   verdict-row consistency lint, adversarial verification, docs audit, and\n   root-clutter checks.\n9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific principle\n   per required field and both convex_factor_run_complete_score and\n   convex_factor_positive_score; preconditions_checked;\n   inference_substrate (small_cpu_input_convex_factor_energy_training);\n   duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows; feature_rows;\n   corruption_rows; split_rows; arm_rows; seed_rows; training_rows;\n   convex_weight_rows; jensen_rows; finite_difference_rows; projection_rows;\n   optimizer_rows; ordering_rows; calibration_rows; size_transfer_rows;\n   latency_rows; baseline_rows; shuffled_label_rows; paired_metric_rows;\n   confidence_interval_rows; label_isolation_rows;\n   fresh_process_replay_rows; checkpoint_paths; r