ission, queue underflow, duplicate debt, poison, contradiction,\n   restart, tombstone, rollback, model hash drift, and aggregate mismatch.\n2. Define MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF and\n   unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Use cached_sota_pair or the current GGUF\n   resolver. Never call AutoTokenizer on a GGUF repository ID. Legacy small\n   models may run CPU smoke tests only and cannot enter headline rows.\n3. Freeze the no-memory, FIFO, and debt-queue policies before inference.\n   Match event order, prompt budget, retrieval count, capacity, decoding,\n   seeds, and total attempted calls. Freeze debt arrival, service,\n   threshold, and drift-plus-penalty coefficient.\n4. Run each model and arm in a separate fresh process. At an event, retrieval\n   may use only earlier exact-success certificates. The current exact\n   outcome becomes visible only after raw output is durable.\n5. For FIFO, admit each exact-success certificate and evict by fixed age.\n   For the queue arm, use only past queue state and certified metadata for\n   admission and retrieval. Never use confidence or rationale as authority.\n6. Charge debt when a retrieved certificate contributes to an exact failure,\n   contradiction, stale use, or retention regression. Apply service only\n   under the frozen rule. Record arrivals, service, balance, decision, and\n   causal source certificate for every event.\n7. Atomically checkpoint raw output, retrieved IDs, prompt hash, exact\n   outcome, write decision, queue state, store hash, tokens, latency, and\n   runtime receipt after each event. Resume at the next missing key.\n8. After the chronological stream, run irrelevant retrieval, delayed-copy\n   poison, contradiction, old-family retention, restart, tombstone, and\n   rollback cases without changing thresholds.\n9. Set queue_learning_run_complete_score=1 when all model, arm, event, and\n   safety rows finish. Set queue_learning_positive_score=1 only when the\n   queue arm beats both n